From 13f1eaf496dadaadad6f699acc762752e7ae59fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James <setkeh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:17:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Forward physical keyboards into native WayVR windows

Native apps launched by WayVR run in its built-in Wayland compositor,
which only receives keys from the in-VR keyboard, so a real keyboard
on the desk can't type into them.

Add an opt-in `physical_keyboard` setting. When enabled, WayVR:

- grabs all physical keyboards (EVIOCGRAB) while keyboard focus is
  on a WayVR window and forwards their keys into the compositor;
- releases the grab and returns focus to the desktop on any physical
  mouse click, so clicking into a window on a real display just works;
- toggles focus between desktop and WayVR on Ctrl+Alt+Escape.

Keys pressed inside WayVR are released when focus leaves, and keys
held across a focus switch don't produce stray releases. WayVR's own
uinput devices are never grabbed. Needs the user in the `input` group.
